Data Analyst Job Market Analysis (SQL Project)

 Overview:
This project analyzes real-world job postings for data analysts using SQL to uncover insights about salary trends, skill demand, and job market dynamics.
The goal is to simulate how a data analyst would:
Clean and structure raw data
Perform exploratory and advanced SQL analysis
Deliver actionable business insights


Objectives:
Identify which skills drive higher salaries
Compare compensation across experience levels
Analyze demand for key tools (SQL, Python, Excel, Tableau)
Explore geographic and remote work trends
Highlight top paying roles and opportunities


Dataset:
The dataset contains job postings with the following attributes:
Job title, company, and location
Salary information
Required skills (SQL, Python, Excel, Tableau, etc.)
Job type (remote/on-site)
Benefits (401k, insurance, etc.)
Posting date (year/month)


Data Preparation:
Data was cleaned and standardized using SQL:
Removed null or invalid salary entries
Standardized categorical fields (job type, region)
Eliminated duplicate records
Structured boolean skill indicators for analysis


Conclusion:
This project demonstrates how SQL can be used to transform raw job posting data into actionable insights, helping both job seekers and organizations make data-driven decisions.

